Let TCP queue 0.25 ms of data below the socket instead of 8 ms.

The driver sets sk_pacing_shift to 7, which lets each TCP socket keep about
8 ms of data queued in the device. Frames are freed as soon as they are
copied into an SDIO aggregate, so that budget sits on top of what the
firmware already holds, and a saturated upload delays everything else on
the link. 12 allows about 0.25 ms. On a PicoClaw that is the knee: a
best-effort ping under a full upload takes 22 ms at 7, 15 ms at 10 and
11.6 ms at 12, with the upload rate unchanged, and 14 gains nothing more.

--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -5870,7 +5870,7 @@
 	rwnx_hw->cmd_mgr = &rwnx_plat->usbdev->cmd_mgr;
 #endif
 	rwnx_hw->mod_params = &rwnx_mod_params;
-	rwnx_hw->tcp_pacing_shift = 7;
+	rwnx_hw->tcp_pacing_shift = 12;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_SCAN
     rwnx_hw->is_sched_scan = false;
